 "notes": "Headline result is the red 'White Dwarfs' excluded region in Fig.1 (MoneyPlotv2, epsilon-model), plane log10(GeV/f) vs log10(m_phi/eV); y-axis GeV/f = 1/f[GeV^-1] = the AxionMass canonical variable. Figure PDF is fully rasterized, so points were read by vision after pixel calibration (x: -20..0 at px195..1711; y: -5..-20 at px61..986.5). Excluded region is a 2D band, so data_points trace the CLOSED boundary polygon (left edge -> top-flat -> upper diagonal frontier -> top plot edge -> right diagonal frontier -> bottom-flat -> close), NOT a single-valued curve. Flat top at 1/f=1.9e-10 (f=5.5e9 GeV) and flat bottom at 1/f=6e-17 (f=1.1e16 GeV) match Eq.(17) f in [5.5e9,1.1e16] GeV (95% CL); the two slope-1 diagonal frontiers correspond to the eps in [2e-20,2e-7] bounds of Eq.(15). Top-right of region extends to the plot top edge (log10(GeV/f)=-4.0); part of the WD region overlaps the Sun (darker red) and SN1987A (brown = red under SN overlay). WD bound does NOT require axions to be dark matter (dm_density null). m_phi is the tuned (exceptionally light) axion mass, decoupled from the canonical QCD mass by epsilon.",
